// Structure navigation marks, including COMPOSITE (multi-word) forms parsed from
// bare tokens: `to coda`, `ds al coda`, `dc al fine`. Segno/Coda targets and
// "To Coda" sit above; the jump-FROM instructions ("D.S. al Coda", "D.C. al
// Fine", "Fine") sit below the staff, right-aligned at the barline (Gould,
// Behind Bars). A mark is an event at a MOMENT, and a section boundary takes no
// time: written before a section (`segno ~B1`) it stands at that section's first
// barline, after one (`~B3 ds al coda`) at the barline that closes it — a text to the
// bar's left, a sign to its right — and the one after the LAST section is drawn too.
// ⚠️ RE-CUT 2026-10-04 (LYS1034, session 793): the marks used to be written inside the
// music (`segno g4 a b c' |`, `g1 | ds al coda`); a navigation mark is form-only now,
// so each bar is a section of its own and the marks stand between the silent references
// (absolute pitches, since the relative frame restarts at every section). The marks stand
// at the barlines the music-level spelling put them at, with the last two texts swapped
// (`fine` before the `dc al fine` that looks for it) so the route reads clean.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/mark-engraver.cc; scm/output-lib.scm.
title "Navigation marks"
time 4/4
octave absolute

part rh { clef treble }

section B1 { rh { g'4 a' b' c'' | } }
section B2 { rh { g'4 a' b' c'' | } }
section B3 { rh { g'1 | } }
section B4 { rh { g'4 a' b' c'' | } }
section B5 { rh { g'1 | } }
section B6 { rh { g'1 | } }

form { segno ~B1 ~B2 to coda ~B3 ds al coda coda ~B4 ~B5 fine ~B6 dc al fine }

score "navigation-marks" { staff rh }
